### Health checks
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### 1) Create a product
# @name createProduct
POST http://localhost:8081/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-1

{
  "name": "Espresso Beans 1kg",
  "price": 24.50,
  "availableQuantity": 10
}

### 2) Place an order (use product id from previous response)
# @name placeOrder
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-demo-001
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-2

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{createProduct.response.body.id}}",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 3) Retrieve the order
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-3

### Idempotent replay (same key + same body) → returns existing order
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-demo-001
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-4

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{createProduct.response.body.id}}",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### Idempotency conflict (same key + different body) → 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: order-demo-001
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-5

{
  "customerEmail": "other@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{createProduct.response.body.id}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}
